{#
  view/j-user/users/delete.phtml — the delete confirmation.

  **This page names the account now, and the .phtml did not.** It filled its `%s` from
  `$this->user->username` — property access on the array `UserTable::getUser()` returns — so
  every render since it was written has asked whether to permanently delete `''`, with a PHP
  warning where the name should be (visible in the capsule, swallowed in production by
  `display_errors = Off`). That is the one difference in this batch taken deliberately: a
  destructive confirmation that names nobody is a safety defect and it is the whole content
  of the page.

  No `headTitle()` in the .phtml, so the browser tab shows the site name alone — hence the
  empty `page_title` from the controller. Empty and not absent: this layout reads
  `page_title` with no `is defined` guard and Twig runs with strict_variables, so omitting
  it renders a 200 with an empty body and no error anywhere.

  The form carries an `action` because the same route serves both verbs and the .phtml sets
  one explicitly.
#}
{% extends juser_layout %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Warning...</h1>
<p>{{ translate("This change is permanent, are you sure you want to delete '%s'?")|format(username) }}</p>
{{ form_open(form, self_url) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('userId')) }}
{{ form_row(form.get('security')) }}
{{ form_submit(form.get('delete')) }}&nbsp;
<a class="btn btn-default" href="{{ juser_path('juser') }}">{{ translate('Cancel') }}</a>
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}
